From 9b2499f668d29bc36f5019038dab329b813952ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MrMao26 <ggonzalez@maoitsolutions.com.ar>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 23:02:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Report the tile the character stands on, not the one it
 reserved

CHARACTER::PositionX/Y is advanced to the *next* path node the moment a
transition starts, not when it ends (MovePath, ZzzAI.cpp). Using it as
the origin of a re-path or as the position reported to the server makes
the client declare ground it has not covered yet.

It compounds, because PathFinding2 resets CurrentPath and
CurrentPathFloat, which re-arms the advance: the next MovePath enters the
advancing branch again. So the declared position moves one tile per
re-emission instead of per tile walked, and re-emissions are paced by
MouseUpdateTimeMax, a frame counter, not by walking speed. At 60 FPS with
a 3-tile path that is one tile declared every 83 ms against one tile
walked every 267 ms - a factor of 3.2, and worse on a faster monitor
because the movement itself is FPS-normalised while the counter is not.

Server side this reads as speedhacking: OpenMU's walk check accumulates
the start positions of recent walk requests and compares the distance
against the elapsed time. Six re-emissions declared six tiles in 500 ms
where 1333 ms were expected, which is enough to exceed the tolerance and,
with the default configuration, ban the account after four warnings.

Add GetCurrentTileX/Y, deriving the tile from Object.Position, and use it
for every path origin, wall trace and outgoing position of the hero.

WHY THE ADVANCE OF PositionX/Y IS KEPT
It is not a bug and it must not be "fixed". MoveCharactersClient builds
the TW_CHARACTER occupancy map out of PositionX/Y, and PathFinding2
consumes that map through iDefaultWall so two characters never path into
the same tile. The advance is what reserves the destination tile for the
duration of the transition. Removing it breaks collision avoidance.
The two meanings simply needed separating: PositionX/Y is the tile we
reserve, GetCurrentTileX/Y is the tile we occupy.

SITES CHANGED  (172 replacements over 118 lines)

  file                  PathFind  SendMagic  PathX[0]  DestValue  CheckWall
  ClassAttack.cpp             11         20         7         10          5
  ZzzInterface.cpp            13          -         2          -          4
  SkillCast.cpp                3          6         -          2          -
  SkillExecution.cpp           1          -         -          -          1

DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED
  ZzzCharacter.cpp, MoveMonsterClient - returns early for the hero; the
    PositionX/Y of other characters comes from the server and is already
    authoritative.
  ZzzInterface.cpp:3328 - compares PositionX against the derived tile on
    purpose, to tell the reserved tile from the occupied one.
  ZzzInterface.cpp proximity checks (abs(c->PositionX - Hero->PositionX)),
    the zone bounds at 2721 and the render helper at 3637 - none of them
    report a position or start a path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
